course: dictionary
lesson: 12087
title: Cloudless skies
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cloudless is made of two parts: cloud and -less. The ending -less means without, so cloudless means without any clouds. A cloudy day has clouds in the sky, and a cloudless day has none at all.
explain: «The sky was cloudless, so the stars shone bright all night.» The clues are the stars shining bright. Stars show best when there are no clouds in the way, so cloudless must mean clear, with no clouds at all.
explain: Stories can use the word differently. «She dreamed of a cloudless childhood» means a happy time with no worries. Here cloudless means calm and untroubled. The feeling of the sentence helps you know which meaning is right.
fact: Cloudless means with no clouds at all; clear.
fact: The ending -less means without, so cloudless is cloud plus less.
fact: «A cloudless sky» means the sky is completely clear.
fact: «A cloudless day» is a perfect day with blue sky and sunshine.
fact: In a story, «cloudless» can mean calm and untroubled, without worries.
exercise: «The children had a picnic under a cloudless sky.» What does cloudless mean? | *With no clouds at all | Lost in the fog | Very windy and wild | Full of dark grey clouds
exercise: «Ben looked up at the cloudless sky and counted the stars.» What does this tell us about the sky? | It is about to rain | It is covered in dark clouds | It is full of smoke | *It is completely clear
exercise: Which part of cloudless shows it means without? | -ud | *-less | cloud | clo
test: «After the storm, the sky was cloudless and blue.» What does cloudless mean here? | *Clear, with no clouds | Full of rain | Covered in grey | Dark and stormy
test: «She felt cloudless happiness on her birthday, with no worries at all.» What does cloudless mean here? | *Calm and untroubled, without worries | Sad and lonely | Covered by clouds | Very noisy
exam: «On a cloudless night, heat escapes into space, so frost can form more easily.» What is the main idea? | Frost never forms on clear nights | *Cloudless nights can be colder, because heat escapes into space | Clouds make the ground colder | Cloudless nights are always warmer
